{"type": "tool_call", "n": 23, "ts": 1790152310.962872, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US MARCH 2026 AP & EXPENSE REVIEW - COMPLETION MEMO\n\nREVIEW COMPLETED: 2026-04-03\nPERIOD: March 2026\nENTITY: US (Halvard Systems Inc.)\n\nSUMMARY OF ISSUES FOUND AND ACTIONS TAKEN:\n\n1. DUPLICATE INVOICE ENTRY - CORRECTED \u2713\n   Issue: JE-00241 (dated 2026-03-05) was a duplicate of JE-00232 (dated 2026-03-03)\n   Invoice: Stackline Cloud STA-98877 - Cloud infrastructure\n   Amount: $31,148.20 (duplicate)\n   Support: Both referenced DOC-0160\n   Action: Reversed JE-00241 via JE-00307 to eliminate duplicate charge\n   Impact: Removes $31,148.20 duplicate expense and AP liability\n\n2. MISCODED EXPENSE - CORRECTED \u2713\n   Issue: JE-00250 incorrectly coded Northgate invoice as \"team dinner\" (Meals & Entertainment - Account 6310)\n   Actual Service: Northgate Data Centers colocation services (NDC-7719)\n   Amount: $3,880.00\n   Support: DOC-0172 invoice clearly states \"Colocation - 2 racks, power and cross-connects\"\n   Action: \n   - Reversed incorrect JE-00250 via JE-00308\n   - Re-posted correctly as JE-00309 to Account 5000 (Hosting & Infrastructure)\n   Impact: Corrects account coding to proper infrastructure expense category\n\n3. UNSUPPORTED PAYMENT - FLAGGED FOR CONTROLLER REVIEW \u26a0\ufe0f\n   Issue: JE-00288 - Legal retainer payment of $6,750.00\n   Date: 2026-03-24\n   Posted by: j.doe (manual entry)\n   Problem: NO supporting documentation attached\n   Status: Exception EXC-001 logged for controller approval\n   Action Required: Controller must provide supporting documentation (engagement letter, invoice, or payment authorization) before this entry can be fully supported\n\n4. POTENTIAL DUPLICATE CHARGE - FLAGGED FOR INVESTIGATION \u26a0\ufe0f\n   Issue: JE-00248 and JE-00249 - Zoom charges\n   Date: Both 2026-03-08\n   Amount: Both $149.90\n   Card: Same corporate card (**** 4417)\n   Support: DOC-0174 and DOC-0175 appear to be identical receipts\n   Status: Exception EXC-002 logged for controller investigation\n   Action Required: Confirm whether these are two separate legitimate charges or a duplicate charge from Zoom\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- AP Account 2000 ending balance: ($100,180.00) - within normal range for March activity\n- All remaining AP entries have supporting documentation\n- Corrected entries properly balanced journal entries posted\n\nCHECKLIST STATUS:\n- \"AP cutoff review\" marked as COMPLETE\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Ensure legal services documentation (EXC-001) is obtained and attached before final close approval\n2. Investigate Zoom card charges with merchant (EXC-002) to resolve potential duplicate\n3. Consider implementing additional controls for manual journal entries to ensure support documentation is always attached at posting\n\nAll correctable issues have been remediated. Two exceptions remain for controller review before final close."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 6}
